{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata","id":1490616,"title":"They were always the Hecata","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-18T08:33:52-07:00","id":1490616,"title":"They were always the Hecata","content":"5th edition V:tM has essentially had the Giovanni fall from full fledged Clan status and created a new Clan of sorts made up of the Cappadocian remnants. It's a pretty radical change. White Wolf doesn't really have the option of a complete retcon, since they want to build off of prior editions and metaplot. However, it seems a bit more logical that the Hecata as presented in V5 always existed as a Clan and that the Giovanni were merely a bloodline of the Hecata.<br /> <br /> This would eliminate rise of the Giovanni and the diablerization of Cappadocius. The Giovanni could still have arisen as a bloodline and family, but never became a Clan, which I feel was too similar to the rise of the Tremere and too total of an elimination of the Cappadocians considering the small and geographically limited nature of the Giovanni.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T09:38:03-07:00","id":1490625,"title":"","content":"As someone who thinks the Giovanni works better than the Cappadocians I would hope that the Cappadocians are not retconned back at the Giovanni's expense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T10:14:55-07:00","id":1490627,"title":"","content":"I always thought the Giovanni were Cappadocians. So the issue of &quot;Hecata&quot; being a &quot;new&quot; clan is besides the point. It doesn't matter if the official clan name changes from Cappadocians to Giovanni to Hecata or anything else. It's always been the same clan, though with various sub-clans/bloodlines.<br /> <br /> This is not a case where someone from another clan diablerized the Antedeluvian (like Tremere and Saulot). Augustus diablerizing Cappadocious is like Gratiano diablerizing Lasombra, or Lugoj diablerizing Tzimisce (let's ignore that they actually did not for the time being). Nobody says that the Lasombra no longer exist and there is only now Clan Gratiano.<br /> <br /> Some might say, &quot;Wait, there is a difference as the Giovanni destroyed the old Cappadocians, and thus now are a new clan!&quot; But that isn't true. Simply killing all the old members does not suddenly transform the new members into a different clan. It's still the same vitae descended from the Antedeluvian. Furthermore, it was never the case that the Giovanni actually destroyed all the old members of the Cappadocians. This was always a timebomb waiting to go off in the setting. No mystery remains anymore. We know the Samedi are also actually Cappadocians. We know there were various other Cappadocians that survived. We know some of the Cappadocians imprisoned during the Feast of Folly survived.<br /> <br /> One unfortunate thing is that the Giovanni clan and the Dark Ages Cappadocians had different Discipline sets. I'll admit this has always bothered me. It also bothered me that Revised would often create sub-clans for many of the clans that also had different Discipline sets. (And that Sabbat versions of clans often did as well.) But by now, we know the Cappadocians had lots of bloodlines (Samedi, Lamia) so calling the Giovanni another isn't much of a stretch.<br /> <br /> Rather than being portrayed as different clans, it'd be more of a case of Cappadocian versus Cappadocian anti-tribu (assigning either name to the Giovanni or the surviving Cappadocians as you see fit, the politics of which group should be the &quot;anti-tribu&quot; is beyond this post). Except that the original clan finally won in the end and destroyed the diablerist.<br /> <br /> If we're to take the setting seriously, the idea that the Giovanni were a new clan was always a pretension. We know that the Giovanni claims to have destroyed the old clan was pitifully wrong. The real issue is that we probably need a revised version of the original &quot;Giovanni Clan&quot; description as presented in the Players Guide and Corebook to represent the actual, real status of the clan, as opposed to the Giovanni propaganda presented in the original. It wouldn't need much change - just a recognition that despite repeated claims of the Giovanni hunting down &quot;the last Cappadocian&quot;, there is ongoing sightings of members of the original clan around the world.<br /> <br /> The issue of whether this group or that one was actually a &quot;clan&quot; or a &quot;bloodline&quot; was often one of semantics. One of the definitions was whether it had a third generation &quot;founder&quot; (as opposed to someone of less potent generation &quot;founding&quot; them), but the more important issue is that other vampires really wanted to keep clans limited to the traditional number of 13. So if the Tremere are clan, it means the Salubri are not. And if Augustus diablerizes Cappadocious and wants to rename the clan, then let him and if surviving Cappadocians don't want to be called that, then I guess it means they are a bloodline. Then the elders shrug and move on to the next topic of conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T10:26:30-07:00","id":1490630,"title":"","content":"I like the Giovanni as metaphor for modern business swallowing up their less efficient and smaller scale predecessors. I also like the eclectic necromancer mix we have as of V20: Incestuous family businesses with varying themes and cultures, the bitter survivors of the purge, the Nosferatu-like Samedi, and the Nagaraja dancing to their own tune. <br /> <br /> Also the Nagaraja aren't even from old Cappa. <br /> <br /> The Hecata? Ehrm... what's the point. They wouldn't function better as a sect and there's no benefit trying to unify the bloodline. I'm all for eating Augustus (it would make a good scenario for players to mess with) but The Hecata just takes away options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T13:01:31-07:00","id":1490648,"title":"","content":"Well the giovanni are a product of the weird gonzo parts of vtm as a more culturally and ethically entrenched clans, the cappadocians later developed on are a more generic death clan I'm guessing heceta is probably white wolfs desire for the 7 non corebook clans to more general archeotypes. Hence why quite a few of the v5 equivalents don't really look like previous editions, heceta as death clan being the most drastic example. <br /> <br /> <br /> Since v5 is a soft retcon, heceta as the historical clan would work as presented just cut out the sub groups and make up your own history.<br /> <br /> Although personally I find pure Heceta a bit bland so you might want to flesh them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-18-2022, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T18:28:02-07:00","id":1490664,"title":"","content":"I don't dislike the idea of the Hecata, at least insofar as the idea of the various necromancer bloodlines coming together to form a powerblock. I don't like all of them turning into the same clan, losing their unique weaknesses and identity however. That's boring. So even in my V20 games I think I'll keep the Hecata around, but as a sect of unique bloodlines. And those bloodlines allow the Hecata to cross over with and have ties to all of the various sects in the setting (Samedi give them an in to the Camarilla, Harbringers give them an in to the Sabbat, Nagaraja an in to the Black Hand, the Giovanni remain as independents, etc). I think that's workable and interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T20:36:23-07:00","id":1490676,"title":"","content":"I do think the almost elimination of the Cappadocians was too contrived a storyline, besides too similar to the Salubri (not in implications, but at least in vibe). I eliminated it in my games long ago, having a far more significant Cappadocian presence in modern nights than the canon.<br /> <br /> But that's about it in my opinion. I think the different weaknesses and Discipline spreads work good enough for the Cappadocian as they came to be, I agree with almost everything <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> said, adding to it <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a>'s that really, unifying mechanics to make them a single clan was boring, not just contrived and silly, but worse still, boring.<br /> <br /> Other than that, the Hecata does make a lot of sense as a coalition. As a clan, though, it has the problem that the groups that form it are really cool and have their own niches, and forcing them into being a single clan just to have only one &quot;Clan of Death&quot; is too limited. The Giovanni aren't the problem. The rest is. Those are some of the most popular and active bloodlines both in-game and irl. They also have some of the most interesting cases of &quot;variations on the same theme&quot;, in that their different takes on Necromancy are, indeed, distinct and flavorful on their own.<br /> <br /> Seriously, as much as I like them, the Giovanni are almost an afterthought in comparison, and that while they're still quite an interesting bloodline, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T05:54:55-07:00","id":1490700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1490676#post1490676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think the almost elimination of the Cappadocians was too contrived a storyline, besides too similar to the Salubri (not in implications, but at least in vibe). I eliminated it in my games long ago, having a far more significant Cappadocian presence in modern nights than the canon.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I tended to imply Cappadocians as bloodline tier still existed in the middle east, India and Africa. With strong links to coptic Christianity as well a number being protected by the setites and assamites respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T06:12:21-07:00","id":1490703,"title":"","content":"As an italian I really miss our bloodspaghetti-eater-necrofuc*ers-mafia in gondola superior Clan status with Skyscrapers in Venice and funny surnames never seen in Venice region.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T14:33:43-07:00","id":1490742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1490664#post1490664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like all of them turning into the same clan, losing their unique weaknesses and identity however. That's boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an inordinate need for setting consistency. So in my chronicles, I ruled that the Giovanni had the exact same Clan Weakness as the Cappadocians. But in addition to that, all the Giovanni ALSO had to take the Flaw Grip of the Damned which gave them the same the weakness as the actual clan weakness (almost, as Grip of the Damned didn't cause an additional health level damage to mortals). It meant all Giovanni characters had two weaknesses, but at least they got 4 additional build points because of it.<br /> <br /> So if you don't mind double dipping, you can easily assign mandatory Flaws to each of the bloodlines. That way you can keep the unique flavor of that lineage.<br /> <br /> Want Samedi to still look like decaying corpses? Give them the Monstrous Flaw.<br /> <br /> Want the Nagaraja line to still consume flesh? Give them the Conspicuous Consumption Flaw.<br /> <br /> Or if you don't think that Flaw really simulates the original weakness or don't like that the Flaws provide different build points, just customize the Curse Flaw (Curse of the Samedi, Curse of the Nagaraja, Curse of the Lamia, and so on) and give each one the same points.<br /> <br /> In my own chronicles, I often have certain Flaws (and sometimes Merits) persist in individual bloodlines within a clan. For whatever reason, their vitae is somehow tainted or special. So if a PC picks something like Repulsed by Garlic, I'll assign that to their sire, grandsire, brood mates, etc. as well. I believe this makes the lineages within the clans more special. So this was an obvious &quot;solution&quot; to making all the Cappadocians have the same Weakness, but still justify the unique flavor for that lineage.<br /> <br /> Although personally, I don't like the Nagaraja being part of the Hecata. Everyone else was at least some spawn of Cappadocious. The Nagaraja had a very distinct origin related to their being a bloodline exclusive to the True Black Hand. And unless one is planning to use that sect, it's best just not to mention the Nagaraja at all.<br /> <br /> However, one thing I do like is that disparate nature of these bloodlines while the Developers and Writers were putting these details down ad hoc had the inadvertent virtue of providing a lot of variety of concepts for a clan of Death that would not have been apparent at the start if you asked someone to design a Clan of Death for inclusion in the game along with the original seven clans. Decadent nobles practicing necromancy, cannibal bankers, priestesses of Lilith, ascetic monks, decayed corpses, and the like showcase how different clan members can be from one another. That's good for inspiration for players seeking to start their first character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 08-19-2022, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T20:56:58-07:00","id":1490752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1490703#post1490703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an italian I really miss our bloodspaghetti-eater-necrofuc*ers-mafia in gondola superior Clan status with Skyscrapers in Venice and funny surnames never seen in Venice region.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not an accurate description, They don't just go around f***ing corpses. They also f*** family! What kind of Italian is you to miss that!?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1490742#post1490742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although personally, I don't like the Nagaraja being part of the Hecata. Everyone else was at least some spawn of Cappadocious. The Nagaraja had a very distinct origin related to their being a bloodline exclusive to the True Black Hand. And unless one is planning to use that sect, it's best just not to mention the Nagaraja at all.<br /> <br /> However, one thing I do like is that disparate nature of these bloodlines while the Developers and Writers were putting these details down ad hoc had the inadvertent virtue of providing a lot of variety of concepts for a clan of Death that would not have been apparent at the start if you asked someone to design a Clan of Death for inclusion in the game along with the original seven clans. Decadent nobles practicing necromancy, cannibal bankers, priestesses of Lilith, ascetic monks, decayed corpses, and the like showcase how different clan members can be from one another. That's good for inspiration for players seeking to start their first character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like it precisely because it better showcases that the Hecata is more a faction than a clan, which is its most interesting aspect to me. So it makes sense that some fringe cases in the faction aren't really related in much more than interests. It also serves as a continuation of their history as a bloodline that has been forced (even if partially) out of their origins.<br /> <br /> Within the original lore, their home was destroyed and they're scattered. If you assume those events not happening, this is still an option to have the members that for any reason went out of the TBH seek refuge. Not only against their former peers, but also because their weakness does create a huge need for support, specially if you take it in the most extreme interpretation.<br /> <br /> And yes, they are a relevant part in the variety of the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T23:22:57-07:00","id":1490766,"title":"","content":"Besides irony , I met some Italians who like the Hecata thing, but all the Italians I know really miss the old Giovanni with their stereotypes and lore. We have this innate skill that allow us to enjoy and laugh at the stereotypes and even make us wanna play them. <br /> The Giovanni are some kind of weird non - existent hybrid of Neapolitan , Sicilian and Venetian stereotypes (very distant regions, by the way) with some necromancy and bad sexual behaviours: this is so crazy that every Italian I know wants to play them and even make them more exaggerated.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni clan managed to do the impossible: the unification of Italy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T02:19:22-07:00","id":1490773,"title":"","content":"I mean hey, why stop at Hecata? Why not do what D&amp;D 5e tried to do and just eliminate Clans altogether? Just select from a preplanned selection of Flaws, roll up three Disciplines you're just happen to start with or whatever, and do everything humanly possible to suggest everyone and everything is equal, no exceptions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T06:12:40-07:00","id":1490779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1490766#post1490766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Giovanni clan managed to do the impossible: the unification of Italy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that's funny. I can't remember the last time a post made me laugh this hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T07:18:01-07:00","id":1490787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1490766#post1490766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides irony , I met some Italians who like the Hecata thing, but all the Italians I know really miss the old Giovanni with their stereotypes and lore. We have this innate skill that allow us to enjoy and laugh at the stereotypes and even make us wanna play them. <br /> The Giovanni are some kind of weird non - existent hybrid of Neapolitan , Sicilian and Venetian stereotypes (very distant regions, by the way) with some necromancy and bad sexual behaviours: this is so crazy that every Italian I know wants to play them and even make them more exaggerated.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni clan managed to do the impossible: the unification of Italy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a slightly weird phenomenon I've noticed were a lot of people will lean into their own peoples archetypes when playing wod. As a Celt I get borderline gleeful playing the most fianna of the fianna-painted blue, running through the woods and full of piss and vinegar, I also had a lot of fun playibg a duncirn giovanni. I have no idea why this is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T07:54:05-07:00","id":1490792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1490787#post1490787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its a slightly weird phenomenon I've noticed were a lot of people will lean into their own peoples archetypes when playing wod. As a Celt I get borderline gleeful playing the most fianna of the fianna-painted blue, running through the woods and full of piss and vinegar, I also had a lot of fun playibg a duncirn giovanni. I have no idea why this is.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an italian from the Alps I get you better than you imagine. Also about the fianna but in a different way. I spent years looking for north italian gallic fianna references : zero except for one mention in a line of the revised tribebook. And still, we are called Gallia Cisalpina.<br /> <br /> Beside that, even if the Giovanni are a stereotype that resemble more the stereotypical southern italian old school loudy mafia man, people from all over italy like to play them. And exactly like they are in the book. I dont know. Italians getting revenge. Pizza mandolino mafia ? YEA EXACTLY BUT THATS THE GHOST OF YOUR MAMMA I JUST DRAINED","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T08:37:09-07:00","id":1490796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1490787#post1490787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its a slightly weird phenomenon I've noticed were a lot of people will lean into their own peoples archetypes when playing wod. As a Celt I get borderline gleeful playing the most fianna of the fianna-painted blue, running through the woods and full of piss and vinegar, I also had a lot of fun playibg a duncirn giovanni. I have no idea why this is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The stereotypes themselves aren't a problem, what's a problem is how they're used, or how they impact your life. That's why the worse reactions tend to be from people living abroad, specially in places where those stereotypes actually inform too much of other's reactions to them.<br /> <br /> I find the lack of representation about other parts of Brazil more annoying than the stereotypes about us, it is less about people getting us wrong and stereotyping and more that I'm really tired of only seeing Rio-based stereotypes plus jungle. But for those living in the US, things are more than a bit more irritating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T09:11:22-07:00","id":1490799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata#post1490616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5th edition V:tM has essentially had the Giovanni fall from full fledged Clan status and created a new Clan of sorts made up of the Cappadocian remnants. It's a pretty radical change. White Wolf doesn't really have the option of a complete retcon, since they want to build off of prior editions and metaplot. However, it seems a bit more logical that the Hecata as presented in V5 always existed as a Clan and that the Giovanni were merely a bloodline of the Hecata.<br /> <br /> This would eliminate rise of the Giovanni and the diablerization of Cappadocius. The Giovanni could still have arisen as a bloodline and family, but never became a Clan, which I feel was too similar to the rise of the Tremere and too total of an elimination of the Cappadocians considering the small and geographically limited nature of the Giovanni.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like both Cappadocians and Salubri survived in much greater numbers than the creators of the game originally intended, at least based on talking to people who were playing when the game first started. Especially the Cappadocians (the Hecata are comprised of like five different bloodlines when originally the whole clan except for the Giovanni were supposed to have been wiped out in the purge).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T16:33:47-07:00","id":1490823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1490792#post1490792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As an italian from the Alps I get you better than you imagine. Also about the fianna but in a different way. I spent years looking for north italian gallic fianna references : zero except for one mention in a line of the revised tribebook. And still, we are called Gallia Cisalpina.<br /> <br /> Beside that, even if the Giovanni are a stereotype that resemble more the stereotypical southern italian old school loudy mafia man, people from all over italy like to play them. And exactly like they are in the book. I dont know. Italians getting revenge. Pizza mandolino mafia ? YEA EXACTLY BUT THATS THE GHOST OF YOUR MAMMA I JUST DRAINED</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought they missed an opertunity to explore lombardi Get of fenris and conflicts with alpine fianna/Roman glass walkers.<br /> <br /> If I ran Italy I'd be tempted to explore the internal tensions between the Venetian giovanni and the sicilian mafia families. I suspect the mafia would despise the clan for both realpolitik and just raw disgust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T16:47:21-07:00","id":1490825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1490823#post1490823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always thought they missed an opertunity to explore lombardi Get of fenris and conflicts with alpine fianna/Roman glass walkers.<br /> <br /> If I ran Italy I'd be tempted to explore the internal tensions between the Venetian giovanni and the sicilian mafia families. I suspect the mafia would despise the clan for both realpolitik and just raw disgust.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Giovanni had a bloodline (the Putanesca, now I think part of the Hecata) who were also a Mafia family.<br /> <br /> Putanesca literally means \u201cwhore\u2019s sauce\u201d in Italian lol. It\u2019s really like a fish-based pasta sauce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T18:07:24-07:00","id":1490831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1490796#post1490796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The stereotypes themselves aren't a problem, what's a problem is how they're used, or how they impact your life. That's why the worse reactions tend to be from people living abroad, specially in places where those stereotypes actually inform too much of other's reactions to them.<br /> <br /> I find the lack of representation about other parts of Brazil more annoying than the stereotypes about us, it is less about people getting us wrong and stereotyping and more that I'm really tired of only seeing Rio-based stereotypes plus jungle. But for those living in the US, things are more than a bit more irritating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soccer, Samba, Carnival and naked asses. Yeah... No. I hate all of those things (well, excluding the naked asses... But I think it's better not discussing that), and therefore Im not particularly found of those stereotypes, even thou I do not care. Oh yes, and jungles. Whatever.<br /> <br /> Im not from Rio de Janeiro, and I really dont care not being &quot;represented&quot;. So I would say that the cartoonish stereotypes are more annoying than being unkown or invisible. But that's of course, me. I do understand your pov thou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 08-20-2022, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T02:01:48-07:00","id":1490853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1490799#post1490799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems like both Cappadocians and Salubri survived in much greater numbers than the creators of the game originally intended, at least based on talking to people who were playing when the game first started. Especially the Cappadocians (the Hecata are comprised of like five different bloodlines when originally the whole clan except for the Giovanni were supposed to have been wiped out in the purge).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's tempting to read the survival of both clans as support for all those players who wanted to be &quot;the last survivor&quot; all those years. The Salubri and Cappadocians were already surviving among the player base, and the plot finally caught up with what many players were doing anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T02:19:16-07:00","id":1490854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1490823#post1490823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always thought they missed an opertunity to explore lombardi Get of fenris and conflicts with alpine fianna/Roman glass walkers.<br /> <br /> If I ran Italy I'd be tempted to explore the internal tensions between the Venetian giovanni and the sicilian mafia families. I suspect the mafia would despise the clan for both realpolitik and just raw disgust.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As a stereotype, we venetians are loudy, workaholic, very xenophobic regarding southeners and kinda separatist. Stuff that can stick perfectly with Giovanni but also Fianna and Get heritages (also historically). ( of course, are we all like the stereotype? Jesus, I hope not...). But I would love also a Shadow Lords presence due to the Republic of Venice and the great ties with eastern europe and Turkey.<br /> <br /> During 70-80-90's here in veneto we had the ''mala del Brenta'', which is also called ''venetian mafia'' but wasn't a true ''mafia'', no family ties and clans. The Mala del Brenta was composed by gangsters, various smugglers that became also drug dealers and black market criminals. I ofter ran the Giovanni with this kind of style instead of the typical mafia thing honestly.<br /> They killed or drove away all the southeners mafiamen that were trying to infiltrate northern italy through public procurement, becoming the n1 criminals not only in Veneto but in the whole northern region with a lot of ties with Slovenia, Croatia and Serbia, maybe even Russia. This is to me what the Giovanni should be in Italy, with various offshot around the nation.<br /> But the whole ''original'' southern mafia looks more like a Brujah thing to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T06:20:31-07:00","id":1490874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1490854#post1490854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As a stereotype, we venetians are loudy, workaholic, very xenophobic regarding southeners and kinda separatist. Stuff that can stick perfectly with Giovanni but also Fianna and Get heritages (also historically). ( of course, are we all like the stereotype? Jesus, I hope not...). But I would love also a Shadow Lords presence due to the Republic of Venice and the great ties with eastern europe and Turkey.<br /> <br /> During 70-80-90's here in veneto we had the ''mala del Brenta'', which is also called ''venetian mafia'' but wasn't a true ''mafia'', no family ties and clans. The Mala del Brenta was composed by gangsters, various smugglers that became also drug dealers and black market criminals. I ofter ran the Giovanni with this kind of style instead of the typical mafia thing honestly.<br /> They killed or drove away all the southeners mafiamen that were trying to infiltrate northern italy through public procurement, becoming the n1 criminals not only in Veneto but in the whole northern region with a lot of ties with Slovenia, Croatia and Serbia, maybe even Russia. This is to me what the Giovanni should be in Italy, with various offshot around the nation.<br /> But the whole ''original'' southern mafia looks more like a Brujah thing to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very I formative.<br /> <br /> I tend not to have any clan/tribe/group as running the irl crime syndicates, usually some guys might be members. I tend to suspect lasombra or ventrue in sicily. But they're topically not calling the shots. Naturally vampires/werewolves/magi who are members deny membership to other supernaturals much like their human counterparts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T02:32:05-07:00","id":1491406,"title":"","content":"Giovanni are also inspired by the Borgia's from Rome. They share the...incestuous thing. And the love for plot an poison.<br /> I'd say they mixed the Borgia's decadent relations, the Mafia's structure from Siciliy, the Venetian merchant's culture, with a bit of financial side from the Medici's family from Flourence.<br /> That said Revised edition did a good job creating strong connections with the Etruscan and Roman (as in Ancient Roman) necromancy.<br /> <br /> (And yeah, being an Italian from Rome I can confirm that Italians do love the Giovanni. But I also understand that for an Italian-American from the other side of the ocean it could reinforce some bad stereotypes about italian descendants).<br /> <br /> And while I have huge problems with V5 metaplot...I like the Hecata, their development and all, for two reasons:<br /> <br /> 1) It was long in the making of the metaplot. Unlike many new things of V5 , it didn't come out of the blue. The notion that there were far more Cappadocians in the world than originally tought was already clear withe the Harbinger of Skull and the Infitiores survived in Egypt (they are a big thing in Cairo by Night). Same as the Giovanni structure crippling (the failure of the great plan after the fifth Maelstrom is a focus of Clanbook Revised). V20 did also a lot of work to bridge these events to the V5, through the revelation that the Cappuchin was a shared identity by Lazarus, Japhet's ghost and Byzar, and the matter of the rebelious lesser branches of the family (Beckett's Diary).<br /> So...it worked, it wasn't really a strange thing happening without reason. And more important: it expaned possibilities.<br /> You still can play Hecata like Giovanni, they are still there, only the higher ups got eaten. But you can play them also like a more Cappadocian mystical clan, or a Voodo Samedi cult. More possibilities, not less. In this regard the operation is kinda similar to what happened to the Assamite in Revised edition. Yeah, you can still play the assassin zealot, but you can also play with the Camarilla, or full indipendent and so on.<br /> <br /> 2) Onyxpath is a better writer, and developer, than the other studios who worked on V5. And Hecata are fully developed by Onyxpath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-26-2022, 05:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T09:21:12-07:00","id":1491771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1491406#post1491406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giovanni are also inspired by the Borgia's from Rome. They share the...incestuous thing. And the love for plot an poison.<br /> I'd say they mixed the Borgia's decadent relations, the Mafia's structure from Siciliy, the Venetian merchant's culture, with a bit of financial side from the Medici's family from Flourence.<br /> That said Revised edition did a good job creating strong connections with the Etruscan and Roman (as in Ancient Roman) necromancy.<br /> <br /> (And yeah, being an Italian from Rome I can confirm that Italians do love the Giovanni. But I also understand that for an Italian-American from the other side of the ocean it could reinforce some bad stereotypes about italian descendants).<br /> <br /> And while I have huge problems with V5 metaplot...I like the Hecata, their development and all, for two reasons:<br /> <br /> 1) It was long in the making of the metaplot. Unlike many new things of V5 , it didn't come out of the blue. The notion that there were far more Cappadocians in the world than originally tought was already clear withe the Harbinger of Skull and the Infitiores survived in Egypt (they are a big thing in Cairo by Night). Same as the Giovanni structure crippling (the failure of the great plan after the fifth Maelstrom is a focus of Clanbook Revised). V20 did also a lot of work to bridge these events to the V5, through the revelation that the Cappuchin was a shared identity by Lazarus, Japhet's ghost and Byzar, and the matter of the rebelious lesser branches of the family (Beckett's Diary).<br /> So...it worked, it wasn't really a strange thing happening without reason. And more important: it expaned possibilities.<br /> You still can play Hecata like Giovanni, they are still there, only the higher ups got eaten. But you can play them also like a more Cappadocian mystical clan, or a Voodo Samedi cult. More possibilities, not less. In this regard the operation is kinda similar to what happened to the Assamite in Revised edition. Yeah, you can still play the assassin zealot, but you can also play with the Camarilla, or full indipendent and so on.<br /> <br /> 2) Onyxpath is a better writer, and developer, than the other studios who worked on V5. And Hecata are fully developed by Onyxpath.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I feel, mostly, too. It was well done; it makes certain rare snowflakes actually *more* accessible, and therefore adds options rather than taking them away; and it's the good sort of streamlining.<br /> <br /> It's also something that had been sort of done in MET V20, where the main clan is Cappdocian, but each sect has a default variant you can play (with rarer versions requiring Merits).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T12:56:30-07:00","id":1491940,"title":"","content":"See, as annoying as it were to have the Giovanni arbitrarily doing their own thing distant away from the rest of kindred society, the old way of doing things was really great for Samedi/HoS/Nagaraja/Other Remnants/Loose necromancers (Do I include the Kiasyd here?) because of course these guys would serve themselves and the option for little-underdog-necromancer made for good fun RP wise. Come the Hecata and everyone who can see ghosts is going to arbitrarily join the big club at the expense of the freedom they had as independents? I don't see the Samedi signing on for it, I don't see the families that were under the Giovanni's thumb into it. I don't imagine how the Nagajara would even recieve the invite. I don't imagine the HoS putting much effort into getting people to toe the line when they've achieved their revenge and are too like the old capadocians to really invest their time in needless politics rather than their own concerns. <br /> <br /> Even agreeing to be represented as one clan to the Camarilla would be a stretch since a hypothetical &quot;Hecata primogen&quot; would very likely favour their bloodline over the others who are direct competitors. Remember, Necromancy is potentially very profitable but it is a niche. Even when they all had different disciplines, the Sephulcre path and a few common rituals is like 80% of why a non-practitioner would want to treat with any of the corpse-fucker varieties. A practitioner's services increase in prestation value when there's nobody else, and decrease in value when other necromancers are around. Smart Giovanni-Nagajara relations would likely boil down to &quot;become my slave and hand over the virteous path and I'll let you live&quot; and something like the Hecata isn't going to alleviate that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T00:32:26-07:00","id":1491988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1491940#post1491940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Come the Hecata and everyone who can see ghosts is going to arbitrarily join the big club at the expense of the freedom they had as independents?</div> </div> </div> </div>Freedom was not the right word.<br /> <br /> 1) The Nagaraja were a broken Clan after the fall of Enoch. They lost their main sect (The True Black Hand) and were in exile. Most of them had to go to South Asia, were the Kue-Jin imposed them a draconian peace treaty (safe harbor, but no right to embrace).<br /> <br /> 2) Same goes for the Harbingers of Skull not aligned with the Sabbat. The nuking of Enoch left them without a home and without political clout.<br /> <br /> 3) Samedi were little fish in a sea full of sharks. Their land, the Carribean Sea, was under Setite's yoke. And plenty of big sharks (Camarilla and Sabbat) set their sight to those lands. They were already looking for the protective umbrella of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> 4) The Infitiores where confined to Saqqara, and they needed the Setite help to survive.<br /> <br /> 5) The branches of the Giovanni's (Dunsinr, Milliners, and so on) had to find a new support after the collpase of the Giovanni's power structure. Otherwise they would have become minor players, like the Revenant families. And that's the best scenario. In the worst they would have been destroyed, like the Pisanob and the Hidalgo.<br /> <br /> So, most of the little necromantic groups had a very precarious situation and where on the verge of crisis at the time of Revised.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't imagine how the Nagajara would even recieve the invite. </div> </div> </div>Nagaraja, being a big part of the True Black Hand, had a lot of dealings with the Byzar, in the persona of the Capuchin. Also, the Harbingers of Skull who are not part of the Sabbat, where members of the True Black Hand. So it probably was something like &quot;Pssst...we are jumping boat! Are you in?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T04:35:26-07:00","id":1491996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1491940#post1491940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, as annoying as it were to have the Giovanni arbitrarily doing their own thing distant away from the rest of kindred society, the old way of doing things was really great for Samedi/HoS/Nagaraja/Other Remnants/Loose necromancers (Do I include the Kiasyd here?) because of course these guys would serve themselves and the option for little-underdog-necromancer made for good fun RP wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you take the Hecata as a clan just as tight-knit as the Giovanni used to be, sure, that would be terrible for them.<br /> <br /> But the main proposal seems to be more of an agreement for mutual survival, and the amount of actual interference on individual actions seems to be low (Capuchin shenanigans aside).<br /> <br /> That simpler take makes a lot of sense and also helps to have them all being easier to fit in a game without need to make them act like best buddies or something. So it fits very well in my book.<br /> <br /> For a Camarilla presence, they could have a council representative or something, it just really matters at the highest level of the organization where most of them won't play anyways and would be barred from even being acknowledged at if they didn't enter. It's like saying that Puerto Rico is better off with an Electoral College they don't have a seat at than an eventual Universal Vote system because they have few people to vote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T06:43:40-07:00","id":1492004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1491988#post1491988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Nagaraja, being a big part of the True Black Hand, had a lot of dealings with the Byzar, in the persona of the Capuchin. Also, the Harbingers of Skull who are not part of the Sabbat, where members of the True Black Hand. So it probably was something like &quot;Pssst...we are jumping boat! Are you in?&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> This is probably the most reasonable way they did it. </span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Freedom was not the right word.<br /> <br /> 1) The Nagaraja were a broken Clan after the fall of Enoch. They lost their main sect (The True Black Hand) and were in exile. Most of them had to go to South Asia, were the Kue-Jin imposed them a draconian peace treaty (safe harbor, but no right to embrace).<br /> <br /> 2) Same goes for the Harbingers of Skull not aligned with the Sabbat. The nuking of Enoch left them without a home and without political clout.<br /> <br /> 3) Samedi were little fish in a sea full of sharks. Their land, the Carribean Sea, was under Setite's yoke. And plenty of big sharks (Camarilla and Sabbat) set their sight to those lands. They were already looking for the protective umbrella of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> 4) The Infitiores where confined to Saqqara, and they needed the Setite help to survive.<br /> <br /> 5) The branches of the Giovanni's (Dunsinr, Milliners, and so on) had to find a new support after the collpase of the Giovanni's power structure. Otherwise they would have become minor players, like the Revenant families. And that's the best scenario. In the worst they would have been destroyed, like the Pisanob and the Hidalgo.<br /> <br /> So, most of the little necromantic groups had a very precarious situation and where on the verge of crisis at the time of Revised.<br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. Everyone's been around long enough to have a few favours owed to them by the Camarilla or Sabbat and they could happily fall in with many cities. Lacking numbers isn't a huge problem for the Samedi or Nagajara, they're bloodlines that work best with smaller groups (especially the Nagajara, given the weakness) , but it's not hard for them to actually have a few more childer if they wished it. Personally I think the Samedi and Nagaraja would have more to gain from closer ties with the Nosferatu (the latter, perhaps, with the Malkavians) or through the Ventrue. I should think fellows like the Milliners who were planning a coup before the one happened had their own out-plan. <br /> <br /> <i>(The Nagajara's aversion to the mainstream sects is pretty silly I think. Once a bloodline gets to a certain size, you can't really tell them how to think) </i><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T10:23:45-07:00","id":1492015,"title":"","content":"The way I see is that the lineages of the Samedi, Infitiores, Harbingers, and Giovanni are still ultimately all derived from the same Antedeluvian. The vitae of Cappadocious is all in their veins. Like it or not, that is the definition of a clan.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly fine for that clan to be heavily divided and not cooperative. The Brujah are famously divided even if they do flashmob when the clan as a whole is threatened. The Gangrel are known for their individualism. Other clans also have deep cleavages. It's really only about which group of elders are in nominal or effective charge. Now its rule by some kind of join committee of elders of all these various bloodlines rather than the whims of Augustus Giovanni.<br /> <br /> The idea that the different Cappadocian bloodlines finally got together and decided to end the Giovanni purge, and start acting as a single clan again - in whatever fashion - seems fine to me. It makes sense. It is even inevitable.<br /> <br /> But the Nagaraja are very different. They have no connection to the Cappadocians (or indeed any other Clans, unlike many Bloodlines, we do know their actual origins). I don't mind if people choose not to use the True Black Hand in their games. But if they don't, there is no reason to utilize the Nagaraja at all. But if for some reason you want to get rid of, but still use the Nagaraja - as the V5 metaplot users want to do - then the newly reformed Cappadocians are not the best place for them. They have nothing in common with them except that they happen to have a unique Discipline that has been retconned into a Path of Necromancy. That is rather poor in-game motivation to join up with some group they have no connection to. It's like saying any sub-clans that now have access to Blood Magic must be part of the Tremere. Or that every clan with Presence must now be considered one clan - Brujah, Toreador, Ventrue, Setites, what's the difference?<br /> <br /> Even if the True Black Hand received a major setback, I don't see why that would compel the Nagaraja to flee to another sect. They are very few in number. The members of the True Black Hand always shifted between Enoch and the mortal world. They already had a network of vampires, ghouls, Revenants, mortals, and other retainers to help them. They can easily hide just like they've always been doing. It's just bad writing to say they simply could not continue on with whatever tasks they already wanted along with any other surviving members of the True Black Hand. And if they did absolutely had to come out of the shadows and join a sect to protect them, I would think the Camarilla would best fit that. It has the greatest numbers and power. Why choose a newly reformed Independent Clan than them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T16:34:56-07:00","id":1492043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492015#post1492015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Nagaraja are very different. They have no connection to the Cappadocians (or indeed any other Clans, unlike many Bloodlines, we do know their actual origins). I don't mind if people choose not to use the True Black Hand in their games. But if they don't, there is no reason to utilize the Nagaraja at all. But if for some reason you want to get rid of, but still use the Nagaraja - as the V5 metaplot users want to do - then the newly reformed Cappadocians are not the best place for them. They have nothing in common with them except that they happen to have a unique Discipline that has been retconned into a Path of Necromancy. That is rather poor in-game motivation to join up with some group they have no connection to. It's like saying any sub-clans that now have access to Blood Magic must be part of the Tremere. Or that every clan with Presence must now be considered one clan - Brujah, Toreador, Ventrue, Setites, what's the difference?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing in common, at all, certainly not the whole study of death and dealings with ghosts.<br /> <br /> They fit perfectly within the Hecata, the only reason against that is the holiness of the metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T16:56:51-07:00","id":1492046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492043#post1492043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing in common, at all, certainly not the whole study of death and dealings with ghosts.<br /> <br /> They fit perfectly within the Hecata, the only reason against that is the holiness of the metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, they fit in perfectly with them so long as you ignore literally everything about them besides the fact they practice necromancy?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T17:34:45-07:00","id":1492052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492046#post1492046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, they fit in perfectly with them so long as you ignore literally everything about them besides the fact they practice necromancy?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bit harsh saying they have absolutely no identity besides their metaplot relevance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T17:55:42-07:00","id":1492053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492052#post1492052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a bit harsh saying they have absolutely no identity besides their metaplot relevance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free to name the ways it is a totally organic move and not just them wanting to streamline necromancy and therefore squishing all necromancers together into a single nonsensical clan.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T18:10:23-07:00","id":1492055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492015#post1492015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if they did absolutely had to come out of the shadows and join a sect to protect them, I would think the Camarilla would best fit that. It has the greatest numbers and power. Why choose a newly reformed Independent Clan than them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Their Clan flaw, needing to eat human flesh, doesn't really fit very well within the Masquerade or upholding Humanity so they wouldn't find themselves welcomed into the Camarilla. They spent centuries as servants to the Antedeluvians so they wouldn't fit in with the Sabbat. Really, it was joining the Hecata or the joining the Anarchs. Joining the Anarchs would have made some sense. The Nagaraja are kind-of-sort-of a Setite bloodline, but they didn't follow Set and so I'm sure the main clan was always looking to destroy them. But the Ministry probably wouldn't care about that. They'd likely be more than happy to have the Nagaraja join up with them, and they'd offer the Nagaraja protection from the main clan.<br /> <br /> But the Nagaraja already had links to the Hecata thanks to their centuries of contact with the Capuchin. And Japeth and Lazarus have some pretty interesting things going on regarding the Underworld, Wraiths and Vampires that I'm sure the Nagaraja are <i>extremely</i> interested in. The Nagaraja were always fairly weird vampires. They were created by a modified version of the Spell of Life, Lichdom and vampiric blood from the Followers of Set. They're likely some sort of proto-type to the Wraith-Vampires that make up the Harbringers of Skulls.<br /> <br /> They have a lot more in common with the Hecata than the Anarchs, and they don't fit in either the Camarilla or the Sabbat, so it seems reasonable that if they were invited by the Capuchin to come join the new sect they'd agree to do so even if they didn't have any direct blood relation. And, considering their skills involving Necromancy, Wraiths and the Underworld, it only makes sense that Lazarus would invite them into his new sect rather than want to see them take all of that knowledge and provide it to someone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-31-2022, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T19:22:35-07:00","id":1492063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their Clan flaw, needing to eat human flesh, doesn't really fit very well within the Masquerade or upholding Humanity so they wouldn't find themselves welcomed into the Camarilla. They spent centuries as servants to the Antedeluvians so they wouldn't fit in with the Sabbat. Really, it was joining the Hecata or the joining the Anarchs. Joining the Anarchs would have made some sense. The Nagaraja are kind-of-sort-of a Setite bloodline, but they didn't follow Set and so I'm sure the main clan was always looking to destroy them. But the Ministry probably wouldn't care about that. They'd likely be more than happy to have the Nagaraja join up with them, and they'd offer the Nagaraja protection from the main clan. </div> </div> </div>Nosferatu are a walking masquerade breach and they still let them join in. Having to eat fresh or well preserved human flesh would be something the Camarilla would definitely put up with to get their own pet necromancers, I think.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T20:56:14-07:00","id":1492065,"title":"","content":"Again, there are several major issues:<br /> <br /> The Nagaraja have to eat human flesh. They can get around 10 days worth of sustenance from one corpse, so each one needs ~35 corpses every year. Those corpses have to come from somewhere, and there's a huge risk for a Masquerade breach if someone finds out corpses are going missing or finds a Nagaraja's larder. Each additional Nagaraja in a city massively increases the risk of discovery. Having to hide, transport and store hundreds of corpses every year is a big logistical problem. I can see a lot of Camarilla Vampires writing the Nagaraja off just for that. Whatever they could provide isn't worth the risk of keeping them around.<br /> <br /> The second is that the Camarilla requires vampires to retain Humanity, but Humanity doesn't work very well at all for the Nagaraja. Those who try and retain Humanity are noted to be feral and very low Humanity. Almost all of them end up on Paths simply because they have no other real choice.<br /> <br /> Those are two massive strikes against them. And while some Camarilla vampires might be willing to welcome a brood of corpse eating feral vampires in exchange for their Necromantic knowledge, I think most of them would say &quot;fuck it, it's not worth it.&quot; Especially since (in 5e) they just got the Lasombra to join, those guys are bringing Necromancy with them and they don't bring any of the problems that the Nagaraja do.<br /> <br /> On the other side, even if the Camarilla offered to allow the bloodline to join, I don't see many Nagaraja accepting. They'd have to get off their Paths and get back onto Humanity and then they'd have to struggle every night to avoid falling to wrightdom. I just can't see the bloodline being willing to waltz with wassail every night in order to join the Camarilla. And what would joining the Camarilla even get them? The Camarilla is a political organization, but the Nagaraja have always been distinctly apolitical. Their interest is primarily in the Underworld and the supernatural. I don't feel that the Camarilla has much that would entice most of them, especially considering the drawback of giving up Paths that would come with joining.<br /> <br /> Honestly between the Camarilla, Anarchs, Sabbat and Hecata I think the Nagaraja would be the <i>least</i> likely to join the Camarilla. At least with the other sects they could maintain their Paths and that's incredibly important for their nightly existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T23:31:11-07:00","id":1492074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492043#post1492043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing in common, at all, certainly not the whole study of death and dealings with ghosts.<br /> <br /> They fit perfectly within the Hecata, the only reason against that is the holiness of the metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you can reduce a clan to solely a specific kind of interest. Are all members of the Path of Death and the Soul in the Sabbat now members of the Hecata too? Do the businessmen of the various Giovanni lineages who are more concerned with business and wealth rather than necromancy now members of the Ventrue? Does every vampire who has some interest in art and culture become automatic members of the Toreador?<br /> <br /> Or since the Nagaraja were originally Mages (Euthanatos) who experimented with vitae and became vampires without being embraced, does that mean they best fit with the Tremere instead? The Nagaraja are skilled Thaumaturgists as well even though it is not one of their in-clan Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Unlike everyone else, the Nagaraja are not descendants of Cappadocious. Could they &quot;join&quot; the reformed clan? Yes. But they could just as easily &quot;join&quot; any other clans who might make good use of them. Or just continue to dwell on the fringes of vampire society since their numbers have always been extremely few and exist as they've always done for the past three thousand years. Unlike some of the rare bloodlines of the True Black Hand (like the True Brujah), there wasn't even rumors about the Nagaraja existing. They were essentially unknown outside that sect.<br /> <br /> The game is in this weird position of basically wanting to disown everything about the Tal'Mahe'Ra in Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, but wanting to keep the IP associated with it so they have to do something with the unique concepts of the True Black Hand. It just creates very odd &quot;continuity&quot; now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T00:01:21-07:00","id":1492076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492065#post1492065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, there are several major issues:</div> </div> </div> </div>There definitely are. So I'm not saying your points aren't valid, but they are some responses that can be given to them. Most of them because of the very gonzo, over-the-top nature of Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand. I understand why the book is not looked upon favorably by many players. I have my own love-hate relationship with it. I like to look at it now more as inspiration for the kind of deep mysteries a chronicle should have, rather than canon that should be accepted unquestioningly. But for the purposes of this thread, I'm going to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492065#post1492065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nagaraja have to eat human flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and all the problems you mentioned exist. But there are some very important caveats. First, the Nagaraja know a Thaumaturgical ritual that allows them to preserve a fresh corpse. This allows them to eat it. They don't need to kill people. They just need access to a morgue, funeral home, or cemetary depending on the exact laws and customs of the place they are in. Take over a place that provides cremation services, and they can easily survive even in countries with modern funeral systems.<br /> <br /> And Nihilistics allows them to feed on wraiths. I think that's stupid myself, but it is canon. Technically it just says they can feed on wraiths like they blood points and doesn't mention the flesh eating aspects, but since this was a signature Discipline of the Nagaraja it was clearly intended for them to be able to do so. So now you don't even need actual corpses for them to feed on.<br /> <br /> Now I know subsequent editions made changes to Nihilistics (I think it may now be known as the Vitreous Path), so this may no longer exist in V5. I know it was still valid in V20. But if so, it's a warning that making so many changes to the original powers and concepts tend to disrupt things as they were originally intended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492065#post1492065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially since (in 5e) they just got the Lasombra to join, those guys are bringing Necromancy with them and they don't bring any of the problems that the Nagaraja do.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair point in V5. But it is also a reason why the metaplot doesn't work unless you want to adopt all of the massive game mechanic changes of V5. If you want to use an earlier rule set, then much of the V5 metaplot just does not make sense. It is not organic as an actual, real setting. It is utterly dependent as a game mechanic and thus artificial.<br /> <br /> The Paths issues I think are more complicated. While the Nagaraja definitely used Paths (and ate human flesh), as members of the True Black Hand they were also paradoxically devoted to protecting humanity from vampires. So their image as being complete monsters is actually contradicted by the tenets of their original sect. There was always this strange mix of the TBH being inhuman yet often humane. And nothing says the Nagaraja can't follow Humanity. The actual character template of a Nagaraja in DSotBH actually had that Path. So it is not any more of an insurmountable issue than it is for all those Path following Sabbat Lasombra who defected in V5. While it seems contradictory for the flesh eating Nagaraja to be on Humanity, you can conceive of them adapting to it given the options they have above on preserving corpses and feeding on ghosts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T00:31:09-07:00","id":1492078,"title":"","content":"While I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> on how relatively easy it would be for the Nagaraja to get into the Camarilla, I mostly agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> on why their joining the Hecata makes sense.<br /> <br /> However the take of the ST on DSotBH, the Nagaraja are characterized as a bloodline that frequently resides <i><b>within the Dark Umbra</b></i>. Even if they don't do that all the time, and some may never go there, that does means that their link to other Necromancers isn't simply a matter of shared Discipline, but <i>in their specific case</i> a matter of literal common ground. Necromancers are more likely than any other vampires to have any kind of contact with them, simply.<br /> <br /> From that comes the rest. While they do fine in low numbers, they also have a higher than average need for a support system due to their need for flesh. Even if they feed from corpses, it still has far more involved logistics than the Kiss, so they need friends with less pronounced needs. Seeking an allegiance that can contribute to their survival seems pretty natural to me, and nothing would be more organic than looking for the people you're more likely to know and them to know you, even if your deeper interests are somewhere else.<br /> <br /> But then, I think as with all the Hecata bloodlines, doubly so for the Nagaraja, the alliance must be seen as a pragmatic partnership and not a dogmatic following, contarry to what other sects are and the TBH even more so. I don't see the Hecata as an institution denying a member the right to participate in another sect, so <i>in this sense</i> they are, indeed, more a clan than a sect. They shouldn't imo be a clan rules-wise, but they're more a support chain than a political or religious affiliation.<br /> <br /> So in this context they make sense. Actually, because of their actual history, most Hecata bloodlines make some sense to be there, and the Nagaraja are actually one of the easiest for me to imagine being there, as they don't have reasons to actually hate others within the group. Although even for those I think the V5 story most flies well enough. The people they really had reason and right to hate got killed in the process, so its a sweet deal, but to me it is ultimately a pragmatic survival deal.<br /> <br /> Not survival in the sense of needed to literally survive, mind you, but survival in the sense of making life safer and easier for each other at a relatively low cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T06:38:11-07:00","id":1492089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492076#post1492076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and all the problems you mentioned exist. But there are some very important caveats. First, the Nagaraja know a Thaumaturgical ritual that allows them to preserve a fresh corpse. This allows them to eat it. They don't need to kill people. They just need access to a morgue, funeral home, or cemetary depending on the exact laws and customs of the place they are in. Take over a place that provides cremation services, and they can easily survive even in countries with modern funeral systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still requires them to eat roughly 3 corpses every month. That's a big Masquerade breach waiting to happen when it comes to collecting, transporting and storing that many corpses. I can't imagine the Camarilla would be too excited at the thought of dealing with the logistics of the Nagaraja. When it comes to Necromancer bloodlines, the Camarilla already has the Samedi, and they don't have the sorts of drawbacks that the Nagaraja bring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492076#post1492076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Nihilistics allows them to feed on wraiths. I think that's stupid myself, but it is canon. Technically it just says they can feed on wraiths like they blood points and doesn't mention the flesh eating aspects, but since this was a signature Discipline of the Nagaraja it was clearly intended for them to be able to do so. So now you don't even need actual corpses for them to feed on.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I would never allow that in one of my games. Nowhere does Nihilistics say that they can treat a Wraith's corpus as flesh for the purposes of their clan flaw. Only that they can treat lost corpus levels as blood. The power even makes a specific comparison to the Kiss. Allowing them to eat wraiths to bypass their clan weakness would definitely be getting into House-rule territory.<br /> <br /> Personally, I feel that requiring them to eat actual corpses is very important to their stories and roles in the game. If they could bypass their clan flaw in such a way they'd pretty much just spend all of their time in the Underworld doing their weird wraithly research and never interact with the larger setting. Instead, they have to leave the Shadowlands and return to the real world on a regular basis to get more bodies to eat. Or, alternatively, they have to be part of an organization capable of transporting bodies across the Shroud for them to eat. Either way requires them to interact with the larger setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492076#post1492076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Paths issues I think are more complicated. While the Nagaraja definitely used Paths (and ate human flesh), as members of the True Black Hand they were also paradoxically devoted to protecting humanity from vampires. So their image as being complete monsters is actually contradicted by the tenets of their original sect. There was always this strange mix of the TBH being inhuman yet often humane. And nothing says the Nagaraja can't follow Humanity. The actual character template of a Nagaraja in DSotBH actually had that Path. So it is not any more of an insurmountable issue than it is for all those Path following Sabbat Lasombra who defected in V5. While it seems contradictory for the flesh eating Nagaraja to be on Humanity, you can conceive of them adapting to it given the options they have above on preserving corpses and feeding on ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the Nagaraja were noted in the books as having a difficult time upholding Humanity as compared to other vampires. It's not impossible for them to remain on Humanity but it's more difficult as a result of both their cannibalism and their Underworld/Necromancy focus as being largely removed from from the day-to-day existence of Humanity. Having to remain on Humanity is going to be a pretty big issue for many of them, and I can't really see what the Camarilla has to offer the Nagaraja that would cause them to be willing to make that sort of sacrifice. And it's a pretty big one.<br /> <br /> Really, what does the Camarilla have to offer them that the Anarchs of the Hecata can't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-01-2022, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T07:51:02-07:00","id":1492092,"title":"","content":"Most of the points I would have made in regards to the Nagaraja have already been made by others here. I've read in other posts that many dislike the combination of Obtenebration with Necromancy, and I have to agree. And I would say the same for Nihilistics.<br /> <br /> Thematically, I see Obtenebration closer to what Nihilistics should have been (as a power that channels Oblivion, not an ersatz-Necromancy), and a new Discipline grouping Obtenebration, Nihilistics, and Daimonion together would have made far more sense to me. That doesn't mean I would lump Lasombra, Nagaraja, and Baali together as a new Clan, although I could see the latter two work out in a way- at least with the more scholary types of the Baali.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T07:54:13-07:00","id":1492093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492089#post1492089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It still requires them to eat roughly 3 corpses every month. That's a big Masquerade breach waiting to happen when it comes to collecting, transporting and storing that many corpses. I can't imagine the Camarilla would be too excited at the thought of dealing with the logistics of the Nagaraja. When it comes to Necromancer bloodlines, the Camarilla already has the Samedi, and they don't have the sorts of drawbacks that the Nagaraja bring.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the bottom line of the Camarilla is that cleaning the messes of your friends is better than cleaning the messes of your enemies. They would accept the Nagaraja for the same reason they accept everyone else (at least originally), because the actual alternative is to have those corpse eaters remaining hidden and causing problems while shitting in the Masquerade through the city without any check until found out, when conflict ensues.<br /> <br /> Welcome them, and instead they'll do their best to help you to keep things clean, including optimize the cleaning of their own needs.<br /> <br /> On what the Camarilla could offer, seriously the same as always and highly dependent on the ST's take on the Camarilla nowadays, but sometimes simply having a peaceful city to live in is good enough, and it is good to remember that the base Camarilla membership isn't a dedicated soldier, just a citizen satisfied at not trying to actively undo the system. If you live in a Camarilla city for any reason, even temporarily, and follow the rules to not get in trouble, for all intents and purposes you're Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Humanity is another take that seriously depends. It is hard for them just because they're used to not be into it. And while the Camarilla discourages other Paths, this is not a law and no one really needs to change if they can follow the law. Also, I thoroughly disagree with the statement that it would be harder for them to follow, however hard the <b><i>logistics</i></b> of their flesh eating are, they have no special requirement to sin against Humanity beyond what feeding on Blood already does, unless you really want to double down on eating fresh from the blood vessel almost every time. Which would be a dumb lifestyle by itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T12:05:26-07:00","id":1492105,"title":"","content":"This makes me think of a nagaraja character who role in the city to is too clean up messy masquerade breaches. Kindred know they are good at getting rid of the bodies, but nobody know how they do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T12:55:02-07:00","id":1492110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492089#post1492089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It still requires them to eat roughly 3 corpses every month. That's a big Masquerade breach waiting to happen when it comes to collecting, transporting and storing that many corpses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily so, as I already explained. I can think of lots of ways a Nagaraja could collect three corpses every month and have no problem maintaining the Masquerade. Lots of people die every day, and some of them are buried in ways that won't prevent a Nagaraja from being able to feed or do some grave robbing. The most obvious example to me was crematoriums. There is no corpse that people expect to see. Mix some blood with ashes of something else, and even forensic tests will provide evidence the ashes were of the corpse in question. And lots of indigents ide whose burials are done by the state with minimal fuss over the presentation of the corpse or any kind of funerals. Take over whatever group handles that, and you can supply a lot of empty coffins. People who donate their bodies to science. Lots of things. Lots of people just disappear and are never found again. <br /> <br /> And these deceptions are only necessary in modernized states. The Nagaraja's home territory is the Middle East. There's probably a lot of places where embalming, supervision of corpses, etc. is not done like it is in the US. Much easier to get access to the newly dead. Since the Nagaraja are clearly inspired by Arabian folklore about ghuls, they just have to resort to typical grave robbing of those stories. Or disguise things to appear that animals were feeding on someone who died in the open. Things that may be a problem in the US or Europe may not be much issues in certain areas elsewhere in the world.<br /> <br /> In other words, I don't see this as an insurmountable obstacle. Lots of ways for a lone Nagaraja to hide their activities. Maybe this comes from playing a lot of Call of Cthulhu scenarios since ghouls are a very popular monster there.<br /> <br /> Obviously their feeding complicates things. Obviously even good arrangements can break down the more Nagaraja there are in a local area. But it doesn't take much imagination to find out a way that the Masquerade is not broken.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, it's not like only the Camarilla cares about the Masquerade. EVERY vampire cares about it. Even the Sabbat. Simply putting the Nagaraja with the Cappadocians does not mean this issue goes away. Whatever solution that works well enough for the Hecata, will work well enough for the Camarilla IMO.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492089#post1492089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I would never allow that in one of my games. Nowhere does Nihilistics say that they can treat a Wraith's corpus as flesh for the purposes of their clan flaw. Only that they can treat lost corpus levels as blood. The power even makes a specific comparison to the Kiss. Allowing them to eat wraiths to bypass their clan weakness would definitely be getting into House-rule territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Nihilistics was not the explicit unique Discipline of the Nagaraja, I would agree with you. But it was given to them. No one else. The powers assigned to it were developed for a reason. It makes absolutely zero sense to give the Nagaraja's unique Discipline a power that could not help them. Especially since the issue of &quot;how do they feed if they spend so much time in Enoch?&quot; is obvious. Allowing them to &quot;eat&quot; ghosts is an obvious solution (even if I find it ridiculous). That the power does not explicitly state the Corpus does not qualify for the Nagaraja I think was just an oversight. That seems the more reasonable explanation to me than the idea this power given to the Nagaraja was incapable of helping them.<br /> <br /> If you don't want to use it in the game - and believe me, I do understand why - then it is just better to not include the Nagaraja either. It's a matched set.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492089#post1492089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I feel that requiring them to eat actual corpses is very important to their stories and roles in the game. If they could bypass their clan flaw in such a way they'd pretty much just spend all of their time in the Underworld doing their weird wraithly research and never interact with the larger setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that has been the explicit depiction of the Nagaraja previously. They were an extremely small Bloodline of a secret sect few knew about conducting netherworld research on a hidden isle in the Tempest. They were never interacting with the larger setting. They were just another gonzo flavor to a sect overflowing with gonzo (Mummies, Mages, more Revenant families, Chatterlings, True Brujah, etc.)<br /> <br /> Unless someone was running a chronicle that dealt with the Tal'Mahe'Ra, the chances of a Nagaraja being in any chronicle was probably near zero (but obviously not zero, I'm sure they have been used in a small number of chronicles). I know that I have never used them when I ST, I've never seen anyone play one in any game, and I've never heard from others of them ever being used. That's just anecdotal evidence, but I have no reason to think I am wrong.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T18:08:08-07:00","id":1492127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492110#post1492110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, it's not like only the Camarilla cares about the Masquerade. EVERY vampire cares about it. Even the Sabbat. Simply putting the Nagaraja with the Cappadocians does not mean this issue goes away. Whatever solution that works well enough for the Hecata, will work well enough for the Camarilla IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again though, it's still an additional difficulty that the Camarilla would have to take on if they wanted the Nagaraja to join. And while I can see some Princes being willing to do so, I can see others refusing to want to shoulder that additional responsibility. This is especially true in 5th edition where the outbreak of the Second Inquisition has pushed maintaining the Masquerade to the top of the Camarilla's priority list. Furthermore the Camarilla has started turning into a reactionary ivory-tower and is more willing to throw those who can't protect themselves to the wolves if it means keeping the rest of the Camarilla members safe. In such a situation, I can't see them as likely to welcome a group that poses a unique threat to the Masquerade like the Nagaraja, or at least I can't see them welcoming the Nagaraja en masse.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Anarchs or even the Sabbat (to some degree) would be more willing to accept them since for them, maintaining the Masquerade is important, but not as important as bolstering their numbers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492110#post1492110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Nihilistics was not the explicit unique Discipline of the Nagaraja, I would agree with you. But it was given to them. No one else. The powers assigned to it were developed for a reason. It makes absolutely zero sense to give the Nagaraja's unique Discipline a power that could not help them. Especially since the issue of &quot;how do they feed if they spend so much time in Enoch?&quot; is obvious. Allowing them to &quot;eat&quot; ghosts is an obvious solution (even if I find it ridiculous). That the power does not explicitly state the Corpus does not qualify for the Nagaraja I think was just an oversight. That seems the more reasonable explanation to me than the idea this power given to the Nagaraja was incapable of helping them.<br /> <br /> If you don't want to use it in the game - and believe me, I do understand why - then it is just better to not include the Nagaraja either. It's a matched set.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, RAW, Consume the Dead only allows a vampire to substitute a wraith's corpus for blood. Nowhere in the power does it say that it allows the vampire to treat wraiths as flesh for the purposes of their clan flaw. It's the Nagaraja signature ability and if it were intended to bypass their requirement for human flesh, the Discipline would have said so. And note that when the Discipline was updated in V20 as a Necromancy Path it still only allowed the user to substitute wraith corpus for blood. Nowhere did it say anything about treating the wraith's corpus as flesh. If you want to allow a Nagaraja with Consume the Dead to treat a wraith's corpus as flesh, you could houserule the Discipline to add that capability to it, and I understand why you might want to do so. But that's outside of the power as written both in DSotBH and in V20.<br /> <br /> Also note that even if you did houserule the Discipline to let Nagraja bypass their clan weakness, the Nagaraja would then have to physically eat a struggling wraith as it writhes in pain. And chowing down on &quot;living&quot; creatures as they scream in agony probably won't do much for that Nagaraja's Humanity rating. That leads to the other problem of the Nagaraja having to give up their Paths and get onto Humanity if they wanted to join the Camarilla. Houseruling it may &quot;fix&quot; the problem of needing to eat human corpses but it's going to exacerbate the problem of trying to stay on Humanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490616-they-were-always-the-hecata?p=1492110#post1492110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless someone was running a chronicle that dealt with the Tal'Mahe'Ra, the chances of a Nagaraja being in any chronicle was probably near zero (but obviously not zero, I'm sure they have been used in a small number of chronicles). I know that I have never used them when I ST, I've never seen anyone play one in any game, and I've never heard from others of them ever being used. That's just anecdotal evidence, but I have no reason to think I am wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience they were a bit more common than that. They were one of the more popular &quot;special snowflake&quot; bloodlines. A Nagaraja even appeared in the Bloodlines video game. Though they didn't necessarily mesh well with most games as PC characters since their clan weakness was kind of icky and didn't work very well with Humanity, which was more or less mandatory for most Camarilla-centric games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-01-2022, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}